<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela's La Seguridad to list on bolsa.</title>
<headline>Venezuela's La Seguridad to list on bolsa.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's largest insurance firm Seguros La Seguridad, majority owned by Spanish insurance group Mapfre, will shortly be listed on the Caracas bolsa, company president Alberto Sosa Schlageter said.</p>
<p>&quot;We have agreed to ask the National Securities Commission for a Caracas bolsa listing,&quot; Sosa told reporters.</p>
<p>Mapfre paid over 3.5 billion pesetas late last year for its 52 percent stake in the company which has a 20 percent Venezuelan market share.</p>
<p>Venezuela's largest bank, Banco Provincial holds a 20 percent share, National Deposits Guarantee Fund Fogade has 13.7 percent and local holding company HL Boulton some 11 percent.</p>
<p>Seguros La Seguridad reported 1996 net profits of 1.7 billion bolivars ($3.6 million) compared to profits of 580 million in 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Ana Isabel Martinez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
